# `Task-decomposition surfaces for issue 847, E57.`
# `Decomposition is a working task like any other, so the surfaces that make`
# `splitting, atomicity and first-step prompts recognisable live here, in seed`
# `data. Following the issue 386 convention the Rust modules`
# `src/task_decomposition.rs and src/solver_handlers/task_decomposition.rs`
# `name only the language-independent roles below; no per-language phrase list`
# `appears in Rust.`
# `The observable and unobservable action pair is the checkability oracle from`
# `the acceptance list. A sub-task is a valid child only when a human can tell,`
# `by looking, whether it is done. Adding a folder to an array is observable;`
# `understanding a codebase is not.`
